{
  "sn47.13:0.1": "Linked Discourses 47.13 ",
  "sn47.13:0.2": "2. At Nāḷandā ",
  "sn47.13:0.3": "With Cunda ",
  "sn47.13:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "sn47.13:1.2": "At that time Venerable Sāriputta was staying in the Magadhan lands near the little village of Nālaka, and he was sick, suffering, gravely ill. ",
  "sn47.13:1.3": "And the novice Cunda was his carer. ",
  "sn47.13:2.1": "Then Venerable Sāriputta was fully extinguished from that sickness. ",
  "sn47.13:2.2": "Then Cunda took Sāriputta’s bowl and robes and set out for Sāvatthī. He went to see Venerable Ānanda at Jeta’s grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "sn47.13:2.3": "“Sir, Venerable Sāriputta has become fully quenched. ",
  "sn47.13:2.4": "This is his bowl and robe.” ",
  "sn47.13:3.1": "“Reverend Cunda, we should see the Buddha about this matter. ",
  "sn47.13:3.2": "Come, let’s go to the Buddha and inform him about this.” ",
  "sn47.13:3.3": "“Yes, sir,” replied Cunda. ",
  "sn47.13:4.1": "Then Ānanda and Cunda went to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "sn47.13:4.2": "“Sir, this novice Cunda says that ",
  "sn47.13:4.3": "Venerable Sāriputta has become fully quenched. ",
  "sn47.13:4.4": "This is his bowl and robe. ",
  "sn47.13:4.5": "Since I heard this, my body feels like it’s drugged. I’m disorientated, and the teachings don’t spr